<title>MEXICO: Banco de Mexico to drain 1.682 bln pesos.</title>
<headline>Banco de Mexico to drain 1.682 bln pesos.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco de Mexico sought to drain 1.682 billion pesos from the secondary market on Monday through a combination of three direct sales of paper and three repurchase agreements, dealers said.</p>
<p>The Cetes sales were assigned as follows:</p>
<p>    AMOUNT     TERM	 AVERAGE RATE</p>
<p>    150 million    346 days   20.97 pct</p>
<p>    150 million    178 days   20.97 pct</p>
<p>    150 million     87 days   20.95 pct</p>
<p>The terms and maturities of the repurchase agreements were offered as follows:</p>
<p>    800 million     31 days</p>
<p>    300 million     21 days</p>
<p>    132 million	1 day</p>
<p>*Amounts in pesos</p>
<p>((--Mexico City Newsroom 525 728-9559))</p>
</text>
